1
00:00:11,034 --> 00:00:14,034
Lucky Face Special Talk

2
00:00:14,034 --> 00:00:16,034
Yay!

3
00:00:16,034 --> 00:00:19,034
Well, but it's still amazing.

4
00:00:19,034 --> 00:00:20,034
It's gorgeous, isn't it?

5
00:00:20,034 --> 00:00:22,034
I'm so happy to see so many people here!

6
00:00:22,034 --> 00:00:25,034
Live Chokoro Takamine no Nadeshiko!

7
00:00:25,034 --> 00:00:27,034
I'm looking forward to working with you.

8
00:00:27,034 --> 00:00:29,034
Please, please, please, please.

9
00:00:29,034 --> 00:00:30,034
Thank you very much.

10
00:00:30,042 --> 00:00:33,582
Let's start by introducing ourselves one by one.

11
00:00:33,582 --> 00:00:36,402
I'm Erisa Higashiyama.

12
00:00:36,402 --> 00:00:39,182
I'm Himeri Komiyama.

13
00:00:39,182 --> 00:00:42,782
I'm Momona Matsumoto.

14
00:00:42,782 --> 00:00:45,582
I'm Sunao Kizuki

15
00:00:45,582 --> 00:00:48,622
Yes, I am Suzumi Suzu.

16
00:00:50,138 --> 00:00:52,138
Yes, I am Hina Hina.

17
00:00:52,138 --> 00:00:55,138
Yes, I am Momoko Hashimoto.

18
00:00:55,138 --> 00:00:58,138
Yes, I am Lili Harana.

19
00:00:58,138 --> 00:01:01,138
Yes, I am Mikuru Hoshitani.

20
00:01:01,138 --> 00:01:03,138
Yes, I am Sahara Hazuki.

21
00:01:03,138 --> 00:01:05,138
Yes, thank you very much.

22
00:01:05,138 --> 00:01:07,138
Thank you very much.

23
00:01:07,138 --> 00:01:09,138
Wow, wonderful. 10 people.

24
00:01:09,138 --> 00:01:10,138
Ten people. Ten people.

25
00:01:10,138 --> 00:01:16,138
Ten people. This may be the largest number of people interviewed in this distribution.

26
00:01:16,138 --> 00:01:18,138
How was this interview?

27
00:01:18,656 --> 00:01:23,656
How was it? It was a downpour at the Lucky Fest.

28
00:01:23,656 --> 00:01:25,656
What did you think of it?

29
00:01:25,656 --> 00:01:28,656
I was looking forward to performing for the first time, but it was too much of a downpour.

30
00:01:28,656 --> 00:01:32,656
I was worried about the fans because it was pouring so hard.

31
00:01:32,656 --> 00:01:37,656
But when we went to the rehearsal, the fans didn't even put on their kappas or anything.

32
00:01:37,656 --> 00:01:41,656
We couldn't do it! It was raining! It was like, "It was raining!

33
00:01:42,112 --> 00:01:48,872
I wanted to do my best to make the show as exciting as the rain,

34
00:01:48,872 --> 00:01:55,232
It had stopped for a little while during the show, so we could see the faces of the fans and enjoyed the show.

35
00:01:55,232 --> 00:01:59,112
Oh, I see. When the show started, it was amazing.

36
00:01:59,112 --> 00:02:00,872
It was amazing.

37
00:02:00,872 --> 00:02:03,612
It was amazing before it started, wasn't it?

38
00:02:03,612 --> 00:02:07,612
What were you guys talking about? Oh my God.

39
00:02:07,612 --> 00:02:10,312
Are we really doing this? Like, "This is impossible.

40
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:12,320
Are you saying, "This is impossible?

41
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:14,320
Well, tell them it's going to be sunny from now on.

42
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:16,320
Oh, there's such a thing as a sunny weather girl?

43
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:19,320
No, we've got two of them.

44
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:21,320
That's a little thin. Two out of ten?

45
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:23,320
Two out of ten?

46
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:24,320
Two out of ten?

47
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:26,320
What? Eight more rainbirds?

48
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:28,320
No, it's just...

49
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:31,320
We always have a pretty good chance of sunshine.

50
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:34,320
Rain was a bit of a bummer. It's been a while since we've had rain.

51
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:38,320
But I guess the two of us have helped weaken it a bit.

52
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:40,320
Weakened.

53
00:02:40,576 --> 00:02:42,522
I'm glad.

54
00:02:42,522 --> 00:02:47,022
Was it easy? Lucky festival. How was it? Everyone.

55
00:02:47,022 --> 00:02:51,022
Yes, everyone shouted a lot,

56
00:02:51,022 --> 00:02:56,522
And since we were allowed to take pictures of Nadeshiko Takamine, people were calling out to us while we were filming,

57
00:02:56,522 --> 00:03:01,522
It was raining, but everyone's voices and energy were so powerful that we didn't feel it,

58
00:03:01,522 --> 00:03:04,522
It was raining, but the energy of the audience was so strong that we felt like we wanted to be a part of the excitement,

59
00:03:04,522 --> 00:03:09,522
We wanted to get excited together with the fans, and I think we were able to get excited together with them on stage.

60
00:03:09,522 --> 00:03:11,522
Didn't you feel the rain?

61
00:03:11,522 --> 00:03:12,464
Rain?

62
00:03:12,464 --> 00:03:22,464
I'm really sorry, but the wind was blowing toward the fans, and it seemed like they were getting more of it than we were.

63
00:03:22,464 --> 00:03:25,464
Really? Not many people came to the stage?

64
00:03:25,464 --> 00:03:27,464
We had to go to the front.

65
00:03:27,464 --> 00:03:30,464
They would see your bangs.

66
00:03:30,464 --> 00:03:32,464
That's what he kept saying.

67
00:03:32,464 --> 00:03:34,464
You don't want that, do you?

68
00:03:34,464 --> 00:03:37,464
It's important. We're missing time.

69
00:03:37,464 --> 00:03:39,464
It was like this, right? That's why.

70
00:03:41,690 --> 00:03:43,690
I thought I didn't have bangs.

71
00:03:43,690 --> 00:03:44,690
I did.

72
00:03:44,690 --> 00:03:45,690
Thank you very much.

73
00:03:45,690 --> 00:03:46,690
That's wonderful.

74
00:03:46,690 --> 00:03:47,690
I saw the whole thing.

75
00:03:47,690 --> 00:03:49,690
Thank you very much.

76
00:03:49,690 --> 00:03:51,690
It was a lot of fun.

77
00:03:51,690 --> 00:03:53,690
I knew it would be more exciting when I got wet,

78
00:03:53,690 --> 00:03:54,690
I get excited when I get wet.

79
00:03:54,690 --> 00:03:55,690
I understand.

80
00:03:55,690 --> 00:03:58,690
It's when you don't want to get wet that the tension goes down the most.

81
00:03:58,690 --> 00:04:02,690
The moment you give up, that's when the fans get excited.

82
00:04:02,690 --> 00:04:04,690
The excitement of the fans when they've had enough.

83
00:04:04,690 --> 00:04:05,690
Yes, it was great.

84
00:04:05,690 --> 00:04:07,690
It was wonderful.

85
00:04:07,690 --> 00:04:09,690
How about Nadeshiko?

86
00:04:09,690 --> 00:04:11,690
Ibaraki is quite like this.

87
00:04:11,696 --> 00:04:14,696
Do you have any connection with Ibaraki? Do you have any connections?

88
00:04:14,696 --> 00:04:15,696
Wow....

89
00:04:15,696 --> 00:04:19,696
Do you have any memories or impressions of Ibaraki?

90
00:04:19,696 --> 00:04:21,696
Yes, it's very personal for me.

91
00:04:21,696 --> 00:04:24,696
My guess is from Ibaraki.

92
00:04:24,696 --> 00:04:27,696
I was at a Tower Records store in my hometown.

93
00:04:27,696 --> 00:04:30,696
Whenever there was a pop-up event at the local Tower Records store

94
00:04:30,696 --> 00:04:32,696
I would go to Ibaraki every time.

95
00:04:32,696 --> 00:04:35,696
I would go to Ibaraki every time and try some of their specialties.

96
00:04:35,696 --> 00:04:36,696
Your guess?

97
00:04:36,696 --> 00:04:37,696
Yes, I did.

98
00:04:37,696 --> 00:04:38,696
Who is your guess in Ibaraki? Takafumi Mito? Who?

99
00:04:38,696 --> 00:04:39,456
Ha-ha-ha-ha.

100
00:04:39,456 --> 00:04:42,416
Who's the house in Ibaraki?

101
00:04:42,416 --> 00:04:46,256
I really like Yori Noguchi from Equal Love.

102
00:04:46,256 --> 00:04:48,876
He's from Ibaraki.

103
00:04:48,876 --> 00:04:51,136
I used to go there every time.

104
00:04:51,136 --> 00:04:53,896
The Ibaraki people are so warm.

105
00:04:53,896 --> 00:04:56,476
When I didn't know the way to get there, I would ask them.

106
00:04:56,476 --> 00:04:58,316
I asked him if he had any good food.

107
00:04:58,316 --> 00:05:00,016
They answered me warmly.

108
00:05:00,016 --> 00:05:03,196
I have an image that the people of Ibaraki are very kind.

109
00:05:03,232 --> 00:05:04,952
I have a great image of Ibaraki.

110
00:05:04,952 --> 00:05:07,112
I guess you have to travel all the way to Ibaraki for your activities.

111
00:05:07,112 --> 00:05:08,112
Yes.

112
00:05:08,112 --> 00:05:11,912
Yes.

113
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:20,380
I had to go to Ibaraki because there was a pop-up featuring my guess and it was only in my hometown, so I wanted to be there.

114
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:31,660
I've been told that every time a cd is released, I'm invited to join the company, so I've been living for that.

115
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:34,400
Please tell me how you feel about being able to sing!

116
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:43,400
Well, I don't know, but I never thought I would be able to perform in Ibaraki Prefecture, and there were so many big artists there today,

117
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:53,400
I never thought I would be able to perform in Ibaraki Prefecture, and there were so many big artists here today, so even when I was walking around, I could hear some of my favorite songs that I had heard before. I am very happy to be able to perform today. Thank you very much.

118
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:59,400
Thank you very much. I wonder if there is only one other person among the 10 who has memories of Ibaraki.

119
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:02,400
It's bad, it's bad, it's bad, it's bad. It's a little bit bad.

120
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:07,480
So what do you think? How's it feel to be here for the first time? How do you feel now? I know it was raining.

121
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:10,480
Of course it was. I'm from Tochigi, too.

122
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:11,480
It's so close!

123
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:12,480
Yes, we're close.

124
00:06:12,688 --> 00:06:23,888
I'm often told that I look like Namari, and I tell people I'm fine, but if I look like someone from Ibaraki, I get comments from fans when I'm distributing.

125
00:06:23,888 --> 00:06:26,428
I get comments from fans when I deliver my messages.

126
00:06:26,428 --> 00:06:28,828
They don't get along with each other because they live next door to each other.

127
00:06:28,828 --> 00:06:29,428
Is that so?

128
00:06:29,428 --> 00:06:31,388
No? Tochigi and Ibaraki are okay?

129
00:06:31,968 --> 00:06:32,988
No, they're fine. - Really?

130
00:06:32,988 --> 00:06:33,868
Really?

131
00:06:34,348 --> 00:06:34,628
Yes.

132
00:06:36,304 --> 00:06:42,124
I've never cared about Ichihara's attractiveness. I've never thought that Tochigi is low.

133
00:06:42,124 --> 00:06:49,024
Tochigi has Nikko, after all. But really, we've been touring for a while, and this is the first time we've come to Ibaraki.

134
00:06:49,024 --> 00:06:55,024
It was the first time for us to come to Ibaraki, so we are very happy to be here for such a big show.

135
00:06:55,024 --> 00:07:01,624
I see. It's what you've always wanted to do. It's big. I've always wanted to perform, so I think the opening act is a very important part of the show.

136
00:07:01,624 --> 00:07:04,080
I think it was the hardest part of the show.

137
00:07:04,080 --> 00:07:10,080
I think it was the most difficult part. It was very exciting, wasn't it?

138
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:14,080
I think it was the hardest part of the show. You just made your debut, right?

139
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:16,080
That's right. It's still a ways to go.

140
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:24,080
It will soon be our second anniversary, and at first I wondered if it would be all right because there were no customers.

141
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:26,080
At the time of your debut?

142
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:28,080
This morning was a bit...

143
00:07:28,432 --> 00:07:34,832
Before the show started, I wondered if it would be okay because it was raining.

144
00:07:34,832 --> 00:07:44,112
But when I went out to the concert, there were so many fans there, and that little antique collector was there, and he was so excited to see me on top of his father, I thought it was a festival.

145
00:07:44,112 --> 00:07:46,932
I felt like it was a festival.

146
00:07:46,932 --> 00:07:51,552
Takarazuka Addisco, do you have more male or female fans?

147
00:07:51,552 --> 00:07:54,490
They're all really supportive...

148
00:07:54,490 --> 00:07:58,210
There are a lot of women who support us.

149
00:07:58,210 --> 00:07:59,670
I'm very grateful.

150
00:07:59,670 --> 00:08:01,870
They all came to the show today.

151
00:08:01,870 --> 00:08:04,050
Even the women.

152
00:08:04,050 --> 00:08:04,550
Women?

153
00:08:04,550 --> 00:08:05,050
Women?

154
00:08:05,050 --> 00:08:05,550
Female?

155
00:08:05,550 --> 00:08:06,050
Female?

156
00:08:06,050 --> 00:08:06,550
Female?

157
00:08:06,550 --> 00:08:07,050
There you go.

158
00:08:07,050 --> 00:08:08,050
Please don't do that.

159
00:08:08,050 --> 00:08:09,050
You're out. You're out. You grew up here.

160
00:08:09,050 --> 00:08:10,050
You're out! You're out!

161
00:08:10,050 --> 00:08:11,050
I'm so glad.

162
00:08:11,050 --> 00:08:14,850
The women wore their hair all back, too.

163
00:08:14,850 --> 00:08:16,050
All back?

164
00:08:16,050 --> 00:08:17,050
She wore her hair all back.

165
00:08:17,050 --> 00:08:18,550
He looked so cool.

166
00:08:18,550 --> 00:08:21,350
I was so happy to see that.

167
00:08:21,350 --> 00:08:23,930
Oh, I see.

168
00:08:23,952 --> 00:08:33,032
I guess it's like you all became idols because you liked it so much in the first place.

169
00:08:33,032 --> 00:08:38,292
Now that we've become idols ourselves, we're the ones that everyone is looking up to.

170
00:08:38,292 --> 00:08:41,072
We're not there yet, not at all.

171
00:08:41,072 --> 00:08:43,072
Not yet!

172
00:08:43,072 --> 00:08:44,452
Not yet!

173
00:08:44,452 --> 00:08:46,452
It's not enough, right?

174
00:08:46,452 --> 00:08:48,452
It's not enough yet!

175
00:08:48,576 --> 00:08:54,216
Are there any artists you want to enjoy or see after this festival?

176
00:08:54,216 --> 00:08:55,976
There are a lot of them.

177
00:08:55,976 --> 00:08:59,116
I really want to eat.

178
00:08:59,116 --> 00:09:02,476
I really want to eat.

179
00:09:02,476 --> 00:09:09,656
I just saw the food menu for the artists backstage.

180
00:09:09,656 --> 00:09:12,696
It looked really delicious, so I want to eat there.

181
00:09:12,696 --> 00:09:14,696
I want to eat rice.

182
00:09:14,696 --> 00:09:16,576
What do you like, by the way?

183
00:09:16,576 --> 00:09:17,836
What? I like...

184
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:19,440
Food...

185
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:20,240
Do you want to introduce yourself?

186
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:22,040
No, I don't.

187
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:24,340
What's your favorite food?

188
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:25,940
Sea eel?

189
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:26,540
Conger eel.

190
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:27,540
I don't have any.

191
00:09:27,540 --> 00:09:28,740
It's not on the menu.

192
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:30,740
No sea eel.

193
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:31,640
Curry...

194
00:09:31,640 --> 00:09:32,540
There was curry!

195
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:34,340
I wanted curry.

196
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:35,440
I wanted to eat Bean-curd soup.

197
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:36,240
Oh, there was...

198
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:36,940
Yes, there was.

199
00:09:36,940 --> 00:09:38,040
Only the sea eel was missing.

200
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:39,640
Damn!

201
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:42,340
Please prepare the sea eel again.

202
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:43,040
It's me.

203
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:45,232
Don't tell me...

204
00:09:45,232 --> 00:09:50,332
I'm a hired MC too. I'm in a position where I could fly away if I blow.

205
00:09:50,332 --> 00:09:54,032
I don't know, but I'm sure we'll have some food afterwards.

206
00:09:54,032 --> 00:09:57,412
Are there any artists you'd like to see? I'm a little concerned about today.

207
00:09:57,412 --> 00:10:03,852
I could hear the rehearsal of Huiyi Ishizaki.

208
00:10:03,872 --> 00:10:08,672
I heard Ishizaki Hyui's rehearsal, but I wanted to go so much I almost skipped the interview.

209
00:10:08,672 --> 00:10:12,172
I was about to skip the interview because I wanted to go to the concert so much.

210
00:10:12,172 --> 00:10:13,872
Shall we end soon?

211
00:10:13,872 --> 00:10:14,872
Yeah, yeah...

212
00:10:14,872 --> 00:10:17,872
But since you weren't here, I'm already at Ganza.

213
00:10:17,872 --> 00:10:19,372
Are you sure?

214
00:10:19,372 --> 00:10:20,072
Of course I'm sure.

215
00:10:20,128 --> 00:10:23,128
I missed you so much. So much. Really? Me? For me?

216
00:10:23,128 --> 00:10:25,128
Thank you. Thank you for the T-shirt.

217
00:10:25,128 --> 00:10:29,128
Thank you very much. I'm sorry, I'm talking about Lucky Face, not Lucky Face.

218
00:10:29,128 --> 00:10:37,128
I'm talking about something other than a lucky face, but... our dressing room is right in the middle of all the other venues.

219
00:10:37,128 --> 00:10:43,128
We can hear the music of many artists. We're on the performers' side.

220
00:10:43,128 --> 00:10:48,128
We were talking about how we want to go here now, looking at the timetable all the time.

221
00:10:48,128 --> 00:10:52,128
So everyone is different? What do you like? Like bands?

222
00:10:52,128 --> 00:10:58,128
But I want to see Kiss of Life. I love K-pop idols.

223
00:10:58,128 --> 00:11:02,128
Yes, they're here. They're here. And they're backstage two doors down.

224
00:11:02,576 --> 00:11:04,576
Two doors down from each other.

225
00:11:04,576 --> 00:11:06,576
Is it possible? I was so excited.

226
00:11:06,576 --> 00:11:08,576
I've been so excited since this morning.

227
00:11:08,576 --> 00:11:10,576
If you put them on the wall like this...

228
00:11:10,576 --> 00:11:12,576
You're pretty close.

229
00:11:12,576 --> 00:11:14,576
I'll just kiss the wall for now.

230
00:11:14,576 --> 00:11:16,576
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

231
00:11:16,576 --> 00:11:18,576
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

232
00:11:18,576 --> 00:11:20,576
You're a sought-after idol, too.

233
00:11:20,576 --> 00:11:22,576
Not at all.

234
00:11:22,576 --> 00:11:24,576
You're really cute.

235
00:11:26,576 --> 00:11:28,576
Is there anyone else you'd like to see?

236
00:11:28,576 --> 00:11:30,576
Maybe someone you haven't talked to yet.

237
00:11:30,576 --> 00:11:32,320
If you don't mind.

238
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:37,600
I'm personally interested in seeing the new school leaders.

239
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:39,180
Nadeshiko from Koya.

240
00:11:39,180 --> 00:11:43,420
Nadeshiko from Takano is making her major label debut with Mr. Entertainment.

241
00:11:43,420 --> 00:11:47,700
We belong to the same company, so we're seniors.

242
00:11:47,700 --> 00:11:51,640
I really wanted to see them live today.

243
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:54,420
I'm sure there are a lot of people like that today.

244
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:55,880
Leaders, right?

245
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:57,820
They're on fences all over the world, aren't they?

246
00:11:57,820 --> 00:11:58,280
Yes, they are.

247
00:11:58,280 --> 00:11:59,280
